### Sample webhooks — VS Code "REST Client" or JetBrains HTTP Client.
### Start the app (npm run dev), then send requests one by one. Outcome: npm run db:report
@base = http://localhost:3000

### S01 exact match → MATCHED (auto)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

< ./fixtures/scenarios/01-exact-match/payload.json

### S04a redelivery of S01 → 200, duplicate (externalId)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

< ./fixtures/scenarios/01-exact-match/payload.json

### S04b same photo, new message id → 200, duplicate (contentHash)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

< ./fixtures/scenarios/04-duplicate-photo/payload.json

### S02 same chain, same amount, same day → NEEDS_REVIEW (NEAR_TIE); logo attachment ignored
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

< ./fixtures/scenarios/02-ambiguous-same-chain/payload.json

### S03 restaurant tip (57.50 vs 63.25) → NEEDS_REVIEW (AMOUNT_TIP_TOLERANCE)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

< ./fixtures/scenarios/03-restaurant-tip/payload.json

### S05 invoice for a transaction that does not exist yet → UNMATCHED (NO_CANDIDATES)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

< ./fixtures/scenarios/05-invoice-no-transaction/payload.json

### S06 unreadable photo → UNMATCHED (NOT_MATCHABLE)
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

< ./fixtures/scenarios/06-garbage-extraction/payload.json

